    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A student keeps one iron nail in dry air and another in moist air. Which nail rusts faster?', '["Nail in dry air","Nail in moist air","Both equally","Neither rusts"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, 'c3af6c75f7fe', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'In electrochemistry, the movement of electrons takes place:', '["Through solution only","From cathode to anode inside solution","During redox reactions","Only in acids"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '4a63e8feffcc', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A laboratory technician coats iron with chromium to make it shiny and corrosion resistant. This process is:', '["Rusting","Distillation","Electroplating","Refining"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '4b309c64d07c', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'Iron pipes buried underground are often attached with magnesium strips. This method is called:', '["Galvanization","Electrolysis","Sacrificial protection","Neutralization"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, 'a006738d77e3', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A student notices bubbles during an electrochemical experiment. The bubbles indicate:', '["Gas formation due to chemical reaction","Melting of metal","Rust prevention","Physical change only"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, '1ab2e30f76f2', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 5, 'A student wants to protect an iron bicycle from rusting. Which method is most suitable?', '["Heating regularly","Keeping in sunlight","Painting surface","Washing with salt water"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, 'dfc70e88507c', null),
